'''''Alpinia''''' is a [[genus]] of [[flowering plant]]s in the ginger family, [[Zingiberaceae]]. Species are native to Asia, Australia, and the Pacific Islands, where they occur in [[tropics|tropical]] and [[subtropics|subtropical]] climates.<ref name=china>[http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=101188 ''Alpinia''.] Flora of China.</ref> Several species are cultivated as [[ornamental plant]]s.<ref name=fna>[http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=1&taxon_id=101188 ''Alpinia''.] Flora of North America.</ref>

==Taxonomy==
The genus was erected by the Scottish botanist [[William Roxburgh]] in 1810, and published in the journal Asiatic Researches.{{R|ROXB}} It is named after [[Prospero Alpini]], a 17th-century Italian botanist who specialized in exotic plants.{{R|S&S}} Species of the genus are known generally as '''shell gingers'''.{{R|fna|ITIS}}

